tcc -run as the whole program of a bare-metal RV64 image (ship-your-tcc c/)

Everything is under #ifdef TCC_BAREMETAL (c/src/tcc-config/config.h), so
the patch changes nothing in other configurations. Applies to tinycc
43c7708 after patches/0001 (the RV64I soft-float code generator).

tccelf.c:
- symbol hash buckets: a mask instead of a libgcc division when the
  bucket count is a power of two (always, for the tables tcc grows).
- tcc_load_object_file: input sections go where GNU ld puts them
  (.text.* into .text, ...), so linking against -ffunction-sections
  archives does not create a section per function.
- tcc_load_alacarte: the archive index is hashed once and each pass looks
  up the undefined symbols in it (upstream looks every index name up in the
  symbol table each pass); same members, possibly another load order.
- tcc_add_runtime: -lgcc after the last -lc (libc.a, libtcc1.a and the
  soft-float code call libgcc's helpers).

tccpp.c:
- predefines newlib's <stdint.h> type macros (__INT8_TYPE__, ...) with
  gcc's rv64 lp64 values.

tccrun.c:
- rt_mem: the run memory is a static arena at a fixed address, the linker
  script's __tccrun_start..__tccrun_end (not .bss: nothing zeroes it), in
  place of mmap/VirtualAlloc/malloc; tcc_run_free does not free it.
- protect_pages: no mprotect (no pages on the bare machine); for the code
  it calls the image's tcc_baremetal_sync_icache (fence.i where supported).
  No <sys/mman.h>.
- tcc_run: before linking, (a) records the size of the program's own code
  (.text so far) and defines __tcc_baremetal_code at its start, (b) adds the
  image's tcc_baremetal_syms (newlib's system-call layer: _write, _sbrk,
  _exit, ...) with tcc_add_symbol, so the program's own copy of libc.a,
  found through the archive loader, runs on the image's HTIF console, file
  system and heap; then calls the image's tcc_baremetal_run (step markers,
  optional code dump) in place of prog_main.
- the CONFIG_TCC_STATIC dlsym table is empty: every symbol comes from the
  program, the archives or tcc_baremetal_syms.

